cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FireViewer software, datasets, models or reproducibility material in research, please cite FireViewer and the specific model/dataset repositories you used."
title: "FireViewer"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Unicorn Who Dev"
    email: "unicornwhodev@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fireviewer"
url: "https://github.com/fireviewer/Fireviewer_doc"
abstract: >-
  FireViewer is open infrastructure for wildfire observation, spatial
  reconstruction, temporal tracking and reproducible post-event analysis. It
  combines provenance-aware evidence handling, headless geospatial production,
  AI-assisted analysis, human review and replayable incident artifacts while
  keeping observed, reconstructed, interpolated, simulated and predicted
  information semantically distinct.
keywords:
  - wildfire
  - geospatial
  - reproducibility
  - computer vision
  - remote sensing
  - open source
  - provenance
  - post-event analysis
